/**
 * @file ft_gguf_kquant_reference_vectors.h
 * @brief GENERATED -- do not edit. K-quant super-blocks and the fp32 words
 *   UPSTREAM GGML produced from them.
 *
 *   Every block is SYNTHETIC: generated from one xorshift32 stream, seed
 *   0x5eed1234 -- ggml's own quantize_row_qN_K_ref over seeded weights,
 *   pseudorandom bytes, and edge cases (all-zero, saturated codes at the
 *   largest finite fp16 scale, negative scales, subnormal scales). No block
 *   comes from a model checkpoint.
 *
 *   Every `expected` word below came out of ggml's own compiled
 *   dequantize_row_qN_K (libggml-base), not out of foundry and not out of a
 *   transcription of ggml. test_convert.c requires ft_gguf_dequant.c to
 *   reproduce all of them BIT-EXACTLY.
 *
 *   Regenerate, from tt/convert:
 *     reference/generate_kquant_reference.sh <llama.cpp checkout>
 *   (the checkout must have build/bin/libggml-base). Committed so the test
 *   needs no ggml.
 *
 * @status None
 * @issues None
 * @todo None
 */

